test(scraper,db): T-403 — M8 and the acceptance run against real Postgres, plus journal drift found doing it

With the owner-approved ipodhan_test available, everything that was PENDING is
now run for real — and running it found more than it proved.

M8 INTEGRATION TESTS: 8/8 against real Postgres (34.9s). ensureRow idempotency,
ensureRow under three CONCURRENT calls, the update patch and its jsonb
round-trip, findDue's inclusion/exclusion, markSuperseded, repointToSurvivor
leaving the colliding row behind, and ON DELETE CASCADE.

DB-BACKED ACCEPTANCE: 8/8, run 1 = 20 network calls, run 2 = 0, with the state
table read back OUT OF POSTGRES (25 state rows, 11 documents rows, FOUND=13
NOT_YET_FILED=12, nothing BLOCKED_ALL). --db now uses a real documents writer
and --reset clears only the four acceptance IPOs, because without it the
persistent state table makes "run 1" cost zero calls and A6/A7 pass vacuously.

THE JOURNAL DOES NOT REBUILD THE SCHEMA. Building from nothing but the journal
exposed drift far wider than the enum collision:
  ipos          journal builds 30 columns incl. a NOT NULL `category` the schema
                no longer has; schema.ts declares 50 with segment/offering_type
  documents     journal builds 7 columns; schema.ts declares ~18
  document_type journal builds 7 values; schema.ts declares 15
Production is fine (built from dumps plus _repair/), but any environment built
from the journal — fresh staging, a CI database, disaster recovery — would
reject every NSE document type the scraper writes.

Repaired here, ENUM ONLY: _repair/2026-08-28_document_type_enum_journal_drift.sql
restores the eight missing document_type values, idempotently, per
drizzle-migration-gated-ddl.md Part D. NOT repaired: the ipos and documents
column drift. That is a schema-ownership decision for the owner, not something
to slip into a document-discovery task, so it is measured and reported
(evidence/T-403/journal-schema-drift.json) rather than silently patched.

The integration test inserts via raw SQL naming only journal-built columns, with
a comment saying why the typed builder cannot be used — so the drift is visible
at the point it bites rather than rediscovered later.

.env.test is gitignored and stays local.
